DESCRIPTION:Voted One of the 35 Most Hilarious Comedians of Diversity by go
 oddeedseats.com in 2018 “I bring the funny” THATGOODFUNNY!\n\nRod Man c
 ertainly does just that. As the winner of season eight of Last Comic Standi
 ng\, RodMan brings an inexhaustible charm\, wit\, an ability to find humor 
 in everyday life with a unique style and delivery to the world of comedy. H
 e has the funny bone of a Southern\, but his act is hilarious from Portland
 \, Oregon to Portland\, Maine and all stops in between.\n\nRod Man's stand-
 up comedy journey began in 1995. Inspired by the comedians he saw on HBO’
 s Def Comedy Jam he signed up for "open mic" nights at Atlanta's Uptown Com
 edy Club. Since those early days... Rod Man has become one of the top stand
 -up comedians in the country performing for sold-out audiences here and abo
 ard. It is often said that he is one of the most underrated comedians aroun
 d and that he should be more of a household name\, to that Rod Man replied 
 “depends on who house you in.”\n\nHe has graced the stages of The World
  Famous Apollo Theater in Harlem\, and The Comedy Store in LA "The Bad Boys
  of Comedy" for HBO\, Martin Lawrence's "First Amendment" for Starz\, Nick 
 Cannon's "Wild 'N Out" for MTV\, "One Mic Stand" for BET\, "The Funny Spot"
  for TV One\, and "The World Stands Up" for BBC America and many more. He g
 raced the big screen in the movie Funny People with Adam Sandler and Seth R
 ogen. He hosted a YouTube show called TimeOut with Rod Man\n\nHe co-hosted 
 a morning drive-time show in Los Angeles on Stevie Wonder-owned KJLH Radio 
 102.3 FM.\n\nRod Man is currently traveling the country honing his stand-up
  skills working on material for future stand-up specials and a new RodCast 
 called Thinking Out Loud with RodMan as well as developing and collaboratin
 g on TV/Film Projects.\n\nThe world is catching on to what true Rod Man fan
 s already know -- he’s a bit eccentric\, down-to-earth\, crazy-funny\, an
 d truly a talented voice in the world of comedy.\n\nHave You Took TimeOut t
 o Laugh Today?\n\nToday’s the…\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/come
 dy-atlas/event/helium-presents-rod-man/
